WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.391
An Orchard Core site that is not installed starts on the Setup screen,

00:00:05.391 --> 00:00:07.991
where a person answers a few questions.

00:00:07.991 --> 00:00:11.457
The Auto Setup module answers them from configuration.

00:00:11.457 --> 00:00:16.310
In this video, you register it, configure it, and watch a site install itself.

00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:24.094
This is the Setup screen of a site that is not installed.

00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:27.410
It asks "What is the name of your site?", then the Recipe and

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.796
the Default Time Zone.

00:00:29.255 --> 00:00:33.809
Next comes "What type of database to use?" Providers that run on a

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:38.995
server also ask for a Table Prefix, a Connection String, and a Table Schema.

00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:42.753
Last is the Super User:

00:00:42.753 --> 00:00:46.673
User Name, Email, Password, and Password Confirmation.

00:00:46.673 --> 00:00:53.338
Auto Setup supplies every one of these answers from configuration, so nobody fills in this form.

00:00:57.538 --> 00:01:00.957
Auto Setup is a setup feature of the host.

00:01:00.957 --> 00:01:07.367
In Program.cs, AddSetupFeatures registers OrchardCore.AutoSetup after AddOrchardCms.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:13.278
The OrchardCore.Cms.Web project in the Orchard Core source does exactly this.

00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:18.181
The module ships with the Orchard Core CMS packages, but the CMS web

00:01:18.181 --> 00:01:22.559
application template does not register it, so you add the call yourself.

00:01:22.559 --> 00:01:25.478
The Features page has no Enable button for it.

00:01:29.678 --> 00:01:36.360
The configuration lives in the AutoSetup section under OrchardCore, for example in appsettings.json.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.088
Its Tenants list holds one entry per site, and exactly one entry must

00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:43.168
have the ShellName Default.

00:01:43.918 --> 00:01:47.412
Each key answers a question of the Setup screen.

00:01:47.412 --> 00:01:54.788
SiteName is the name of your site, and AdminUsername, AdminEmail, and AdminPassword describe the Super User.

00:01:55.538 --> 00:02:00.804
RecipeName is the name of a setup recipe, such as Blog, Agency, or SaaS.

00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:03.032
It is not the display name:

00:02:03.032 --> 00:02:07.082
the Setup screen shows Software as a Service for SaaS.

00:02:07.082 --> 00:02:12.078
SiteTimeZone is a time zone identifier, such as America/Los_Angeles.

00:02:12.828 --> 00:02:19.301
DatabaseProvider is Sqlite, SqlConnection for SQL Server, MySql, or Postgres.

00:02:19.301 --> 00:02:24.605
Every provider except Sqlite needs a DatabaseConnectionString.

00:02:24.605 --> 00:02:29.128
DatabaseTablePrefix and DatabaseSchema are optional.

00:02:33.328 --> 00:02:38.737
The section holds an administrator password, and a connection string for most providers.

00:02:38.737 --> 00:02:44.433
In production, supply them as environment variables, where a double underscore separates each

00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:47.368
level and array items are numbered from zero.

00:02:48.118 --> 00:02:53.025
During development, user secrets keep the values out of source control.

00:02:53.025 --> 00:02:58.569
The dotnet user-secrets command takes the same keys, separated by colons, and the

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:02.138
OrchardCore.Cms.Web project has a user secrets ID.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.173
This host has the configuration and no data.

00:03:09.173 --> 00:03:12.796
Let's request its home page, which starts the installation.

00:03:13.261 --> 00:03:17.932
The installation ran during that request, and Auto Setup redirected the browser to

00:03:17.932 --> 00:03:19.365
the root of the site.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:24.088
The navigation bar shows the SiteName from the configuration, and the content comes

00:03:24.088 --> 00:03:25.521
from the Blog recipe.

00:03:25.979 --> 00:03:29.175
Let's open the login page, and log in with the user name and

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.209
the password from the configuration.

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:36.206
In the admin, Settings, General shows the Site name and the Default Time

00:03:36.206 --> 00:03:38.418
Zone that the configuration set.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.386
The Setup screen uses the same setup service.

00:03:45.586 --> 00:03:48.345
The Tenants list can hold more sites.

00:03:48.345 --> 00:03:53.414
When Auto Setup installs the Default tenant, it also creates a tenant for

00:03:53.414 --> 00:03:58.162
every other entry, routed by its RequestUrlHost or RequestUrlPrefix.

00:03:58.162 --> 00:04:01.306
Each one installs on its own first request.

00:04:02.056 --> 00:04:06.987
By default, the first request to a tenant starts its installation.

00:04:06.987 --> 00:04:10.616
When AutoSetupPath is set, only that path does:

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:17.396
/autosetup for the Default tenant, and /harbor/autosetup for a tenant with the prefix harbor.

00:04:21.596 --> 00:04:24.631
Auto Setup validates its configuration first.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:28.976
When a required key is missing, or there is not exactly one Default

00:04:28.976 --> 00:04:32.071
tenant, it logs the errors and does not start.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:35.106
It acts only on sites that are not installed.

00:04:35.856 --> 00:04:43.013
When an installation succeeds, an Information level log entry names the site that Auto Setup provisioned.

00:04:43.013 --> 00:04:48.428
When it fails, for example because the database is unreachable or the password

00:04:48.428 --> 00:04:54.166
is rejected, the response is 503 Service Unavailable, and the log lists the errors.

00:04:54.916 --> 00:05:00.112
When several instances share one database, register the Redis Lock feature as a

00:05:00.112 --> 00:05:03.597
setup feature too, and set the Redis configuration.

00:05:03.597 --> 00:05:08.426
The instances take the lock one at a time, so the site is installed once.

00:05:09.176 --> 00:05:11.519
The lock options are optional.

00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:18.615
When you set LockOptions, give both LockTimeout and LockExpiration a value above zero, in milliseconds.

00:05:18.615 --> 00:05:23.236
Without LockOptions, a distributed lock uses 60 seconds for each.

00:05:25.236 --> 00:05:29.463
Auto Setup answers the questions of the Setup screen from configuration.

00:05:29.463 --> 00:05:34.016
Register it in the host, describe each tenant, keep the secrets in environment

00:05:34.016 --> 00:05:37.647
variables, and the site installs itself on its first request.

00:05:37.647 --> 00:05:39.056
Thanks for watching.

